it's probably okay to just leave the errors as they are and not spend too much time fixing them.

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:57.150
There's certainly no harm to going into your training set and reexamining the labels and

00:01:57.150 --> 00:02:02.190
fixing them. Sometimes that is worth doing. But your algorithm might be okay even if you don't,

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:08.750
so long as the total data set size is big enough and the actual percentage of errors is,

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:13.950
you know, maybe not too high. So I see a lot of machine learning algorithms that are trained even

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:19.870
when we know that there are few mistakes in the training set labels and usually it works okay.

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:28.910
There is one caveat to this, which is that deep learning algorithms are robust to random errors.

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:38.750
