due to incorrect labels. Whether Y value in your depth set was wrong and that accounted for Y

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:30.750
you're learning algorithm made the prediction that differed from what the label on your data says.

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:36.670
So the question now is, is it worthwhile going in to try to fix up,

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:44.350
you know, this 6% of incorrectly labeled examples? My advice is if it makes a significant difference

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:48.910
to your ability to evaluate algorithms on your depth set, then go ahead and spend the time

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:53.630
to fix the incorrect labels. But if it doesn't make a significant difference to your ability

00:04:53.630 --> 00:04:58.670
to use the depth set to evaluate classifiers, then it might not be the best use of your time.

