0.6% of your overall errors are due to incorrect labels. So now if you were to examine a set of

00:06:45.310 --> 00:06:52.270
mislabeled depth set images, so that comes from just 2% of depth set data you're mislabeling,

00:06:52.830 --> 00:07:01.790
then a very large fraction of them, 0.6 divided by 2%, so that's actually 30% rather than 6%

