00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:32.590
and try to fix up some of the labels, here are a few additional guidelines or principles to consider.

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:39.710
First, I would encourage you to apply whatever process you apply to both your depth and test

00:08:39.710 --> 00:08:45.310
sets at the same time. We've talked previously about why you want your depth and test sets to

00:08:45.390 --> 00:08:49.790
come from the same distribution. The depth set is sort of telling you where to aim the target,

00:08:49.790 --> 00:08:55.470
and when you hit it, you want that to generalize to the test set. So your team really works more

00:08:55.470 --> 00:09:00.510
efficiently if the depth and test sets come from the same distribution. So if you're going in to

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:04.750
fix up your depth set, I would apply the same process to the test set to make sure that they

00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:09.630
