isn't always easy to do, so it's not always done. The reason it's not always done is because

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:11.950
if your classifier is very accurate, then it's getting a lot fewer things wrong than right. So

00:10:11.950 --> 00:10:17.870
if your classifier has your 98 percent accuracy, then it's getting 2 percent of things wrong and

00:10:17.870 --> 00:10:24.350
98 percent of things right. So it's much easier to examine and validate the labels on 2 percent of

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:30.830
the data, and it takes much longer to validate the labels on 98 percent of the data. So this

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:38.000
